WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.675
[opening theme song playing]

00:45.086 --> 00:46.629
PATIENT NAME
LEE MYUNG-HAN

00:48.047 --> 00:50.425
There's an arrest warrant out
for Mr. Lee Myung-han.

00:50.508 --> 00:53.011
Charges are extortion and insurance fraud.

00:53.094 --> 00:55.388
[tense music]

01:13.406 --> 01:14.365
[sighs]

01:16.242 --> 01:18.119
He's in his room right now.

01:18.203 --> 01:20.038
A biopsy found he has…

01:21.581 --> 01:22.665
lung cancer.

01:23.541 --> 01:26.086
[Si-woo] They'd like to run
more tests tomorrow.

01:27.670 --> 01:31.049
If you still have to take him in,
do what you have to do.

01:35.970 --> 01:36.930
[detective sighs]

01:39.849 --> 01:41.142
[detective] Ugh, what a headache.

01:41.851 --> 01:43.686
- Constable Kim.
- [Constable Kim] Yes, sir?

01:43.770 --> 01:46.898
Go talk to, uh, whoever doctor's on call.
Find out if we can arrest him

01:46.981 --> 01:48.942
- or if we'll have to wait.
- [Constable Kim] Yes, sir.

01:49.025 --> 01:49.859
[detective] Mm-hm.

01:52.529 --> 01:54.197
ULTRASOUND ROOM

01:55.824 --> 01:57.867
Miss Chae Yu-jin's guardian can come in.

01:57.951 --> 01:59.577
- Yes?
- [assistant] We're ready for you.

01:59.661 --> 02:00.703
Oh.

02:01.579 --> 02:05.333
[doctor] So, your stomach is tightening.

02:05.416 --> 02:07.585
It's really quite common.

02:07.669 --> 02:10.964
As your uterus is expanding
to make space for the baby.

02:11.798 --> 02:15.260
Thankfully,
your baby's absolutely perfect.

02:20.098 --> 02:21.266
And let's see.

02:21.850 --> 02:24.269
I'll find the heartbeat for you, too.

02:24.352 --> 02:25.937
[monitor trills]

02:26.020 --> 02:28.690
[heart thumping]

02:32.610 --> 02:34.612
[soft music]

02:44.998 --> 02:46.040
[chuckles softly]

02:54.632 --> 02:57.510
[Ha-kyung] Sometimes,
choices that seem so obvious

02:57.594 --> 03:00.430
suddenly change
and become impossible to make.

03:15.820 --> 03:18.573
When you can't do
what you think you need to,

03:19.073 --> 03:20.992
there's no way to go forward.

03:21.993 --> 03:23.536
But you can't go back, either.

03:26.372 --> 03:28.416
[soft music]

03:38.801 --> 03:40.762
The officers left.

03:40.845 --> 03:42.972
They need the doctors to sign off,

03:43.806 --> 03:46.226
and he won't
until the testing is complete.

03:47.352 --> 03:48.311
[sobs]

03:50.230 --> 03:51.272
So…

03:52.148 --> 03:54.943
were you able to talk to your dad at all?

03:55.902 --> 03:57.237
[breathes sharply]

03:59.822 --> 04:01.407
Si-woo, are you crying?

04:02.116 --> 04:04.786
[sniffling]

04:05.370 --> 04:07.330
I'm okay. I just need space.

04:11.251 --> 04:13.753
Anyway, we're not in the office,
we don't have to pretend.

04:16.589 --> 04:18.758
You don't need to act like you care
how I'm doing.

04:19.968 --> 04:20.969
Director.

04:21.052 --> 04:22.262
[sobs]

04:22.345 --> 04:24.806
[somber music]

04:29.811 --> 04:32.021
[Ha-kyung] Even if we're not sure

04:32.105 --> 04:36.317
which choice is right
or which will do the least damage,

04:36.401 --> 04:39.320
we still have to decide, to make a choice.

04:39.946 --> 04:41.864
We try to do what is right

04:42.824 --> 04:46.119
to live up to the right expectations.

04:46.744 --> 04:47.954
THIS SPRING

04:48.037 --> 04:49.080
Here.

04:51.165 --> 04:52.625
[clicks tongue]
How's work?

04:53.793 --> 04:55.878
Sir, what's your secret? How do you do it?

04:57.088 --> 04:59.340
Hm? My secret?

04:59.424 --> 05:02.969
Your forecast are the most accurate
statistically in all of the KMA.

05:03.052 --> 05:04.804
No one else even comes close.

05:04.887 --> 05:07.682
You… You're a living legend, really.

05:07.765 --> 05:09.767
You've made history.
So, how do you get it right?

05:10.351 --> 05:12.103
Hmm…
[clicks tongue]

05:12.186 --> 05:14.522
Sounds like you should be
trying harder, hm?

05:14.605 --> 05:17.525
I set the record ages ago,
and no one's come close?

05:17.608 --> 05:18.568
That's just sad.

05:18.651 --> 05:21.321
You could tell me your secret
to getting it right,

05:21.404 --> 05:23.364
then see if I can break your record.

05:23.448 --> 05:24.407
Huh?

05:25.199 --> 05:27.535
What do you think? Do you wanna know?

05:28.244 --> 05:30.496
Yes. I'd really like to know.

05:30.580 --> 05:31.873
Would you tell me, sir?

05:33.124 --> 05:34.751
[sighs]
Okay, then.

05:34.834 --> 05:36.627
You'll find out if you figure out

05:36.711 --> 05:39.047
who has the worst forecast history
at the KMA.

05:39.881 --> 05:40.715
What?

05:43.009 --> 05:45.011
Figure that mystery out,
and you'll know my secret.

05:45.094 --> 05:46.179
Okay?

05:46.262 --> 05:48.514
[gentle music]

05:50.266 --> 05:57.023
EPISODE 16
TOMORROW'S ANSWERS

05:57.106 --> 05:59.067
FINALE

05:59.150 --> 06:01.027
[door lock chimes]

06:04.447 --> 06:07.700
- [door closes]
- [door lock chimes]

06:16.417 --> 06:17.502
You're late.

06:18.336 --> 06:24.759
Oh, well, they changed the forecast
and I had to smooth things over.

06:28.846 --> 06:29.680
Sorry.

06:30.723 --> 06:32.892
[breathes deeply]

06:32.975 --> 06:35.061
You must be tired. Get some sleep.

06:36.229 --> 06:37.271
Hyang-rae.

06:41.651 --> 06:42.735
What?

06:45.113 --> 06:46.989
Should… Should we divorce each other?

06:48.282 --> 06:49.200
What?

06:51.327 --> 06:54.205
I was just thinking on my way coming here,

06:55.832 --> 06:57.875
what Bo-mi wanted was so sad to me.

06:57.959 --> 06:59.961
All she asked for was a dinner

07:00.044 --> 07:02.463
where we would go out on her birthday
and eat together.

07:03.923 --> 07:08.928
And even then, I'm so pathetic
that I can't manage one dinner.

07:13.057 --> 07:15.268
That might be the best that I can do.

07:15.351 --> 07:17.437
[somber music]

07:27.947 --> 07:29.949
[playful music]

07:39.709 --> 07:40.668
All right.

07:43.045 --> 07:46.674
- What do your parents do for a living?
- Huh?

07:46.757 --> 07:48.342
You're doing it again, Mother.

07:48.426 --> 07:49.635
[Seok-ho clears throat]

07:50.678 --> 07:53.055
Both my parents worked as teachers
when I was a kid.

07:53.681 --> 07:57.351
My father thought high school physics
and retired two years ago.

07:57.435 --> 07:59.896
My mother is still working.
She's a vice-principal now.

08:00.521 --> 08:04.150
Oh, so education runs in your family.

08:04.233 --> 08:05.443
Tell me about yourself.

08:05.526 --> 08:07.528
Where did you get your degree?

08:07.612 --> 08:09.614
I majored in physics at Hanguk University.

08:09.697 --> 08:12.825
Oh, Ha-kyung went to that school.
Did you know that?

08:12.909 --> 08:14.952
Yes. I was way before her, though.

08:15.036 --> 08:16.287
Oh.

08:17.246 --> 08:19.582
And this apartment…

08:19.665 --> 08:20.833
I own it.

08:20.917 --> 08:24.504
Uh, I haven't completely paid off
the mortgage yet,

08:24.587 --> 08:26.088
but it… it's in my name.

08:27.006 --> 08:32.136
I know that your work is fairly stable.
You own this place, so you're ready.

08:32.220 --> 08:33.679
All that's left is the wedding.

08:33.763 --> 08:36.849
- Huh?
- Ah, Mom! Mom, don't say things like that.

08:37.433 --> 08:40.019
You always go way too fast.
You'll scare him away.

08:40.102 --> 08:42.855
- Oh, I wouldn't say that.
- I'm sorry, Mr. Shin.

08:42.939 --> 08:45.066
Don't worry about anything.
She does this all the time.

08:45.149 --> 08:47.860
[Tae-kyung] Marriage is all
she ever wants to talk about.

08:47.944 --> 08:50.363
That's why Ha-kyung moved out
to live on her own.

08:51.030 --> 08:54.534
Well, there's, um, expectation
that you'll get married one day, right?

08:54.617 --> 08:56.577
- No way.
- [nervous chuckle]

09:00.164 --> 09:03.417
We aren't expecting it?
Not even in the future?

09:03.501 --> 09:07.171
We… We weren't even close to that stuff.

09:11.259 --> 09:13.094
[whispers]
Then why did you sleep with me?

09:14.095 --> 09:17.014
When two people date
and it goes well, they do that.

09:18.224 --> 09:23.271
It's not what we were doing.
We were just sleeping together. Right?

09:23.354 --> 09:26.023
You and me, it was a real thing, yeah?

09:26.691 --> 09:28.776
We connected together, didn't we?

09:28.859 --> 09:32.822
And we felt, uh… love. Beyond that, we…

09:32.905 --> 09:34.865
It wasn't just physical for us.

09:34.949 --> 09:36.951
No, no, no. Hey, hey. Stop it, stop it.

09:37.034 --> 09:40.454
This is something for you two
to figure out privately.

09:40.538 --> 09:41.831
I thought…
[nervous chuckle]

09:43.374 --> 09:44.959
You are my first…

09:45.042 --> 09:46.669
First one. And I…

09:46.752 --> 09:50.715
Jin Tae-kyung, you are my first love,
you are my first everything.

09:50.798 --> 09:52.091
Oh.

09:52.174 --> 09:53.509
Well, well, so what?

09:53.593 --> 09:55.177
I'm responsible for you now?

09:55.261 --> 09:56.721
I'll go. I've heard enough.

09:56.804 --> 09:59.140
Were you playing with me?
I'm a toy to you?

09:59.223 --> 10:00.683
The fact that you'd even say that!

10:00.766 --> 10:02.184
I'm not that kind of girl!

10:02.268 --> 10:04.353
You were just gonna go all the way
with someone you didn't wanna marry?

10:04.437 --> 10:06.272
I liked you. I do like you.

10:06.355 --> 10:08.399
That's why we dated,
and why we went all the way!

10:08.482 --> 10:09.400
- [Seok-ho] I can't believe this.
- I'm sick here.

10:09.483 --> 10:11.569
I thought you liked me
and you were serious!

10:11.652 --> 10:12.945
I do like you!

10:13.029 --> 10:15.823
- But you said you don't want to marry me.
- That's right. I don't want to!

10:15.906 --> 10:17.074
- It doesn't…
- [groans]

10:17.158 --> 10:19.410
- [door closes]
- Oh, jeez!

10:20.286 --> 10:21.912
[both sigh]

10:26.250 --> 10:29.670
[reporter] Gusts of cold wind are
bringing down temperatures even further.

10:29.754 --> 10:32.840
Right now, let's take a look at Seoul.
Currently, 3 degrees Celcius.

10:32.923 --> 10:35.134
This evening, we'll see things deep
below freezing.

10:35.217 --> 10:37.887
Thankfully, it will rise back
above zero tomorrow morning.

10:37.970 --> 10:39.680
We'll get that warm weather back.

10:39.764 --> 10:40.640
[sighs]

10:47.188 --> 10:48.189
Yu-jin.

10:48.272 --> 10:50.691
- Hm?
- [Ki-jun] I remembered it.

10:51.484 --> 10:52.360
What?

10:52.443 --> 10:55.237
The exact day, the very moment
I started loving you.

10:57.865 --> 11:02.203
[indistinct chatter]

11:03.663 --> 11:04.705
[Yu-jin] Excuse me.

11:05.206 --> 11:07.083
What's an area of dense temperature?

11:08.584 --> 11:10.211
There was a part of the briefing.

11:10.294 --> 11:13.589
Oh, it was talking about the warm air
being introduced to the west coast.

11:14.757 --> 11:17.301
It's where the isothermal lines
are concentrated.

11:17.927 --> 11:19.804
Oh, that makes sense.

11:22.098 --> 11:25.935
Okay, what about the relationship between
the vertical structure of temperature

11:26.018 --> 11:27.269
and the water equivalent?

11:27.353 --> 11:29.814
I wasn't able to find it. Could you…

11:31.232 --> 11:34.819
The vertical structure has information
like vertical temperature

11:34.902 --> 11:36.320
and humidity of a certain area.

11:37.238 --> 11:38.364
[Yu-jin] And so…

11:38.864 --> 11:42.034
You fell in love with me
and thought I was an idiot?

11:42.618 --> 11:43.661
No.

11:43.744 --> 11:44.870
Then what?

11:44.954 --> 11:47.123
It was just the way
you looked at me that day.

11:47.206 --> 11:49.250
[gentle music]

11:51.001 --> 11:53.712
If you look here, you can see
if the numerical development

11:53.796 --> 11:55.089
is gonna be strong or not.

11:55.172 --> 11:57.758
And whether the structure
is one where the water content

11:57.842 --> 12:00.136
will allow the snowflakes to grow.

12:04.974 --> 12:07.268
[Ki-jun] You looked at me
in this way that…

12:07.351 --> 12:08.394
[Yu-jin] Oh.

12:10.646 --> 12:13.524
[Ki-jun] …made me feel like
I could do anything if you were there.

12:20.448 --> 12:21.657
In that moment,

12:22.491 --> 12:25.202
I felt like I was doing everything
I should be doing.

12:25.870 --> 12:26.912
[sucks teeth]

12:26.996 --> 12:29.498
I could tell. I could see it in your eyes.

12:30.833 --> 12:34.336
"Wow, there isn't anything
he doesn't know."

12:34.920 --> 12:37.131
"He's such an expert,
I could ask him anything,

12:37.214 --> 12:38.924
well, about weather."

12:39.008 --> 12:42.470
"And he doesn't talk down
to anyone with a question."

12:43.095 --> 12:43.929
"What a stud."

12:46.557 --> 12:47.808
That's how I felt.

12:51.520 --> 12:52.897
Could you believe in me

12:54.440 --> 12:56.775
in that way about things today?

12:59.737 --> 13:02.490
It's not enough,
'cause it's about reality.

13:03.657 --> 13:05.326
A kid isn't something to do, just 'cause…

13:06.702 --> 13:07.661
I know.

13:08.245 --> 13:10.623
You should see
my search history this week.

13:11.457 --> 13:14.418
- Kids are really expensive.
- I know that, too.

13:15.002 --> 13:16.837
It's not just us, though.

13:16.921 --> 13:18.923
Everyone has to deal with this.

13:19.006 --> 13:21.842
They all have kids anyway,
and they all seem just fine.

13:21.926 --> 13:23.719
Why shouldn't we do it, too?

13:26.388 --> 13:27.681
Honestly, Yu-jin,

13:29.141 --> 13:31.936
when we heard the heartbeat yesterday,

13:32.561 --> 13:34.522
my heart could've burst out of my chest.

13:36.482 --> 13:39.860
It felt like the first time
our kid was talking to the two of us.

13:42.446 --> 13:43.781
Saying that it's here.

13:44.990 --> 13:46.158
That it exists.

13:48.994 --> 13:52.039
And I felt like I wanted to say something.

13:54.959 --> 13:56.377
"That's right, kid."

13:57.336 --> 13:58.337
"Hello."

14:00.297 --> 14:01.882
"This is your dad speaking."

14:02.508 --> 14:04.760
[gentle music]

14:08.055 --> 14:09.139
[inhales sharply]

14:16.814 --> 14:17.648
Yu-jin.

14:18.399 --> 14:19.942
I will do better

14:20.442 --> 14:22.861
for you and our kid's sake.

14:26.156 --> 14:27.116
Hm?

14:29.326 --> 14:30.828
[sniffles]

14:37.126 --> 14:38.460
[sighs]

14:38.544 --> 14:39.795
Thank you.

14:45.676 --> 14:46.719
[sniffles]

14:48.053 --> 14:49.430
I love you.

14:49.513 --> 14:50.806
[chuckles softly]

14:52.600 --> 14:53.893
I love you too.

14:56.312 --> 14:57.563
[sobbing]

14:58.397 --> 14:59.732
[chuckles softly]
You too.

15:10.075 --> 15:11.911
[breathes deeply]

15:11.994 --> 15:14.997
I'm gonna be a father now. Got to provide.

15:15.080 --> 15:17.833
So get it together and do
what you've got to do.

15:18.834 --> 15:20.085
[exhales deeply]

15:20.169 --> 15:22.713
PENSION CREDIT APPLICATION FORM
FOR CIVIL SERVANTS

15:23.839 --> 15:26.383
- [employee 1] You're sure about this?
- What?

15:26.467 --> 15:29.261
When you take out pension credit,
you're using the money

15:29.345 --> 15:32.806
for your retirement in advance.
I don't see anyone using their pension.

15:34.642 --> 15:37.061
[Ki-jun] I'm a father now. Got to provide.

15:37.144 --> 15:39.897
So get it together and do
what you've got to do.

15:40.856 --> 15:43.192
- My wife is having a baby.
- Oh!

15:43.275 --> 15:45.611
So, we need to move
and we need to prepare.

15:46.195 --> 15:48.280
And my credit's limited from another loan.

15:48.364 --> 15:50.616
- Oh, I see.
- [Ki-jun] Yeah.

15:50.699 --> 15:51.700
[mumbles]

15:52.910 --> 15:55.579
[employee 1] Here, you can print out
everything you'll need

15:55.663 --> 15:58.165
for your application
from our website online.

15:58.248 --> 16:00.918
If you have any questions
or need assistance, just reach out.

16:01.001 --> 16:02.628
- We're here for you.
- Thanks very much.

16:03.253 --> 16:04.088
You've got this.

16:05.172 --> 16:07.007
Yes. Got it. Thank you.

16:11.220 --> 16:12.680
LOAN POLICIES AND PROCEDURES

16:14.223 --> 16:15.599
[exhales deeply]

16:24.441 --> 16:26.402
[employee 2]
Is Lee Si-woo getting married?

16:26.485 --> 16:27.486
[employee 1] What?

16:28.153 --> 16:30.698
[employee 2] He was asking
all about getting a housing loan.

16:30.781 --> 16:32.950
- What else could it be for?
- What?

16:33.033 --> 16:35.077
So Jin Ha-kyung
will finally get her wedding?

16:35.160 --> 16:37.788
I guess. They're going fast, huh?

16:39.331 --> 16:41.875
Unless… she's pregnant?

16:41.959 --> 16:44.253
[employee 2 gasps]
That would explain why.

16:44.336 --> 16:45.713
[employee 1] Yeah, it does.

16:45.796 --> 16:47.631
[employee 2] Oh!

16:47.715 --> 16:49.508
Huh? She's pregnant?

16:50.551 --> 16:52.136
According to the Management team.

16:52.219 --> 16:54.054
[scoffs]
No way.

16:54.972 --> 16:56.306
[approaching footsteps]

16:57.391 --> 16:59.268
One iced Americano and…

16:59.935 --> 17:02.438
- Actually, lemon tea, and that's it.
- [employee 3] Okay.

17:04.648 --> 17:05.899
- [Myung-ju] Director.
- Oh.

17:06.775 --> 17:08.277
You don't want coffee today?

17:08.902 --> 17:11.071
Oh, the special's lemon tea, so…

17:11.155 --> 17:14.116
- Ah.
- Oh, yeah, right. Good choice.

17:14.199 --> 17:16.368
The tea has more vitamins in it.
You'll be needing those.

17:16.452 --> 17:18.912
- Here's the citrus tea you ordered.
- [Ha-kyung] Thank you.

17:19.538 --> 17:20.789
All right, I'm heading upstairs.

17:20.873 --> 17:21.915
- Yeah, okay.
- Okay.

17:23.834 --> 17:26.211
[Sung-jin] Wow, she's already
being so careful.

17:27.254 --> 17:30.174
'Cause you're not supposed
to have caffeine when you're pregnant.

17:30.257 --> 17:33.469
- Isn't that right, Mrs. Oh?
- Oh, we don't know anything for sure.

17:33.552 --> 17:35.637
Don't tell anyone else till we know.

17:35.721 --> 17:36.638
- Okay.
- See you.

17:36.722 --> 17:37.598
Mm-hmm.

17:39.892 --> 17:40.809
[sighs]

17:42.186 --> 17:43.562
Hey, have you heard?

18:10.339 --> 18:11.882
[all] Hello, everyone!

18:12.466 --> 18:15.719
[employee 4] These are the new candidates
during the KMA field training.

18:15.803 --> 18:17.971
We're here to observe
the forecast meeting today.

18:18.639 --> 18:20.099
[all] Nice to meet you.

18:20.182 --> 18:22.184
- Great.
- Nice to meet you.

18:22.267 --> 18:24.394
You look so young. Nice to meet you.

18:25.062 --> 18:27.523
- All right. Let's get out of the way.
- Come on.

18:30.901 --> 18:32.820
[Soo-jin] I remember those days.

18:34.238 --> 18:36.198
Yeah? You miss it?

18:37.074 --> 18:40.828
I thought I'd do big important assignments
each and every day.

18:41.495 --> 18:43.622
And now? The magic went away?

18:44.873 --> 18:45.958
Well…

18:46.750 --> 18:48.418
It's not what I expected.

18:48.502 --> 18:50.212
I keep making mistakes.

18:50.295 --> 18:51.755
Even when I really try.

18:52.422 --> 18:53.841
If it's not what you want.

18:54.508 --> 18:56.885
Go somewhere that wants you.
You shouldn't wait it out.

18:59.680 --> 19:01.223
Why are you telling me this now?

19:02.975 --> 19:04.309
Because I know.

19:04.393 --> 19:06.770
The Policy Department
wants you to transfer.

19:08.355 --> 19:09.231
Mrs. Oh…

19:09.314 --> 19:11.984
And I know I should be asking you to stay.

19:12.568 --> 19:14.778
But I know better than anyone here

19:14.862 --> 19:18.115
that forecasting is thankless
and almost impossible.

19:18.198 --> 19:19.867
All-nighters are coming

19:19.950 --> 19:22.744
and the public still complains
even though we work so hard.

19:22.828 --> 19:25.205
I really don't want
to tell you what to do.

19:26.915 --> 19:28.458
[Myung-ju breathes deeply]

19:28.542 --> 19:30.502
So, think about it.

19:31.128 --> 19:32.963
You should just do what you want.

19:33.046 --> 19:34.006
Hm?

19:36.633 --> 19:38.886
[tender music]

19:49.229 --> 19:51.398
Mr. Lee Myung-han, let's change your IV.

19:56.778 --> 19:59.406
[Ha-kyung] It's expected to develop
as it moves over the ocean,

19:59.489 --> 20:02.951
so it should primarily affect
only the southern regions.

20:03.035 --> 20:06.455
We're expecting around 5mm
of precipitation all around the country

20:06.538 --> 20:09.041
in the weekend,
with the rain hitting Chungnam first.

20:09.124 --> 20:12.878
Please keep an on eye surface temperature
and relative humidity in our major areas.

20:12.961 --> 20:15.422
- That would be all. Thank you for coming.
- [cell phone buzzing]

20:16.173 --> 20:17.049
[Bong-chan] Good work.

20:17.132 --> 20:18.926
[all] Good work.

20:20.177 --> 20:21.637
[phone buzzing]

20:23.388 --> 20:24.723
[Bong-chan grunts]

20:25.849 --> 20:27.476
[Team Leader 1] Oh, Director Jin.

20:28.435 --> 20:30.354
- Congratulations.
- What?

20:30.437 --> 20:31.813
[Team Leader 2] Congratulations for what?

20:31.897 --> 20:34.775
- I heard the good news, is it true?
- You heard good news?

20:34.858 --> 20:37.027
It's okay, we already know.

20:37.110 --> 20:39.404
- Do you have a date picked out?
- [Team Leader 2] Really?

20:39.488 --> 20:42.532
Wow, we'll be invited
for a wedding dinner at least, right?

20:42.616 --> 20:44.159
[Team Leader 1] Right, Director Jin?

20:44.243 --> 20:47.329
- Careful he eats a ton.
- [laughter]

20:52.125 --> 20:53.877
A wedding? For who?

20:55.379 --> 20:56.964
Wait, my father is not there right now?

20:57.047 --> 21:01.134
Yes. He-- He wasn't in his room earlier,
so we searched the building.

21:01.218 --> 21:03.262
We think he's left the hospital.

21:03.345 --> 21:04.388
He didn't contact you?

21:04.972 --> 21:05.889
No.

21:07.933 --> 21:10.769
Thank you for alerting me.
I'm sure that he must be nearby.

21:11.770 --> 21:12.688
[breathes heavily]

21:14.564 --> 21:15.607
[inhales nervously]

21:16.233 --> 21:18.235
FATHER

21:19.653 --> 21:21.154
[line beeping]

21:21.947 --> 21:24.324
[operator] The person you are
trying to reach is unavailable…

21:25.993 --> 21:27.995
[tense music]

21:30.622 --> 21:32.499
What? From which office?

21:32.582 --> 21:36.628
Uh, it must've been from Management
when Si-woo asked about the housing loan.

21:37.337 --> 21:41.091
Si-woo's getting a housing loan,
and that means we're getting married?

21:41.842 --> 21:42.801
Well…

21:43.343 --> 21:45.595
Why else would a guy want a loan
to get a house?

21:45.679 --> 21:48.473
Plus, it's Si-woo,
who everyone knows is dating you.

21:48.557 --> 21:50.225
They connect the dots, and there you go.

21:51.518 --> 21:52.686
Still, I wish they…

21:53.895 --> 21:56.023
Why is Si-woo getting
a housing loan, then?

22:06.616 --> 22:08.660
Lee Si-woo is not at his desk?

22:08.744 --> 22:10.162
He just left, but he has his phone.

22:11.163 --> 22:12.414
So then, are you…

22:13.790 --> 22:16.001
gonna do it for real?

22:17.169 --> 22:18.378
What am I going to do?

22:18.462 --> 22:19.671
The wedding.

22:20.714 --> 22:22.841
Ah! That's ridiculous.

22:22.924 --> 22:27.054
So then, you're not pregnant,
either, are you?

22:27.137 --> 22:28.805
Why would you think that?

22:28.889 --> 22:31.141
Well, since everyone was saying
you're getting married,

22:31.224 --> 22:33.185
they thought you could be.

22:33.268 --> 22:36.354
And you had lemon tea this morning,
instead of coffee, so…

22:37.314 --> 22:38.482
Oh, the tea?

22:39.357 --> 22:40.192
Ah!

22:41.610 --> 22:45.030
Mrs. Oh. I won't have a baby anytime soon.

22:45.530 --> 22:49.451
Lee Si-woo's housing loan doesn't have
anything to do with me or us, either.

22:49.534 --> 22:53.080
So, please don't read into things.
If I have news, you'll know.

22:53.955 --> 22:55.040
[Ha-kyung scoffs]

22:56.708 --> 22:57.584
In fact…

22:59.336 --> 23:01.379
[sighs]
There's something I need to tell you.

23:01.463 --> 23:02.881
Mr. Lee and I…

23:04.174 --> 23:05.467
stopped seeing each other

23:06.551 --> 23:08.678
[mellow music]

23:10.764 --> 23:12.974
Honestly, we broke up
after the last typhoon.

23:13.058 --> 23:15.268
We were worried
about what everyone would say

23:15.352 --> 23:18.855
and thought it'd be easier
to put off telling everyone, but…

23:21.233 --> 23:22.859
It just isn't working, so…

23:23.819 --> 23:26.571
Lee Si-woo and I broke up.

23:28.698 --> 23:30.492
We're sorry for not telling you sooner.

23:34.454 --> 23:36.873
[mellow music]

23:47.509 --> 23:48.510
You heard that?

23:49.970 --> 23:50.804
Yeah.

23:51.888 --> 23:53.723
Okay. So the act's over.

24:01.481 --> 24:02.399
[sighs]

24:02.482 --> 24:04.484
[mellow music]

24:09.364 --> 24:11.283
So it's over for them, too.

24:12.200 --> 24:13.410
[clicks tongue]

24:14.202 --> 24:15.036
[sighs]

24:16.371 --> 24:18.748
PETITION FOR DIVORCE

24:26.631 --> 24:28.508
Why were you looking at that?

24:28.592 --> 24:31.428
Mom, you're gonna do it?

24:32.888 --> 24:34.222
Your father said it's best.

24:34.306 --> 24:36.391
I thought you were going to
give him two months.

24:37.058 --> 24:38.018
You changed your mind?

24:38.768 --> 24:40.353
Your father changed his mind.

24:40.437 --> 24:41.646
What about you?

24:42.606 --> 24:44.065
Mom, do you want a divorce?

24:51.990 --> 24:52.908
Can't you…

24:54.826 --> 24:56.494
Don't you wanna know what I think?

24:59.456 --> 25:01.625
- What are you saying?
- Don't I get an opinion?

25:01.708 --> 25:05.170
Shouldn't I get the say
whether you leave him or not?

25:05.253 --> 25:06.504
You told me to.

25:07.088 --> 25:08.798
You said to divorce him if I wanted to.

25:08.882 --> 25:11.259
I hadn't spent time with Daddy,
I didn't know.

25:12.135 --> 25:12.969
What?

25:13.053 --> 25:15.055
Now, I don't want him to go.

25:16.681 --> 25:19.226
I don't want him to go back
to living alone.

25:20.393 --> 25:21.811
So, please.

25:21.895 --> 25:23.855
Can you forget it and let him come back?

25:25.899 --> 25:28.568
You can't hate him that bad. Do you?

25:31.321 --> 25:32.572
You got school.

25:33.156 --> 25:35.200
[somber music]

25:40.330 --> 25:42.999
It's between us.
We're the parents. We'll decide.

25:44.167 --> 25:45.585
Ma.

25:46.836 --> 25:48.421
Have some food and get to school.

25:53.176 --> 25:55.804
Bo-mi, you have to eat.

25:55.887 --> 25:57.180
- Bring a snack.
- [door opens]

25:58.348 --> 25:59.391
[door slams]

26:06.648 --> 26:07.524
[sighs]

26:09.985 --> 26:11.611
This is awful.

26:15.782 --> 26:18.868
Director Jin, I heard the good news.

26:18.952 --> 26:20.912
Uh, no. Oh no. I'm not getting married.

26:20.996 --> 26:22.080
We broke up.

26:24.791 --> 26:26.084
[employee 5] Director Jin--

26:26.167 --> 26:28.169
I'm not getting married. We broke up.

26:30.338 --> 26:32.048
- This is not true.
- Really?

26:32.132 --> 26:34.217
[upbeat music]

26:37.220 --> 26:39.431
[sighs]
Office romance will be the death of me.

26:45.812 --> 26:48.356
- I'd like to eat alone.
- I came here to brag.

26:49.357 --> 26:51.359
Ugh, you don't know how to read the room?

26:53.778 --> 26:55.405
[heartbeat playing]

26:55.488 --> 26:56.656
What is this?

26:56.740 --> 26:58.950
It's the baby. We heard the heartbeat.

26:59.826 --> 27:00.952
Wait.

27:03.413 --> 27:04.414
I saw it as well.

27:04.497 --> 27:06.916
- Oh! Oh?
- [Ki-jun chuckles]

27:07.000 --> 27:08.376
Is it actually this loud?

27:08.460 --> 27:10.587
- It was. Said the doctors.
- [gasps]

27:12.464 --> 27:14.716
- [chuckles]
- Han Ki-jun.

27:19.179 --> 27:20.930
Why do you lash out like that?

27:21.765 --> 27:22.974
Like what?

27:23.058 --> 27:26.353
You didn't have to make a big scene
dumping Si-woo with everyone there.

27:26.436 --> 27:27.937
[breathes heavily]

27:28.021 --> 27:29.272
I just told the truth.

27:29.898 --> 27:31.608
It's been over since the typhoon.

27:31.691 --> 27:33.318
Are you sure that's what he meant?

27:33.401 --> 27:34.402
What are you saying?

27:34.486 --> 27:37.989
Si-woo said all that how you
should pretend you were still together.

27:38.073 --> 27:41.076
I think it's 'cause he didn't want it
to be over between you.

27:41.659 --> 27:43.036
Which is pathetic, but…

27:43.119 --> 27:45.622
I think he just wanted to hold on to you
however he could.

27:47.290 --> 27:49.542
- Let's change the subject.
- [Ki-jun] Lee Si-woo…

27:51.628 --> 27:53.171
must still really love you.

27:58.635 --> 28:00.970
- I'm just gonna eat.
- [Ki-jun] And I think you do, too.

28:03.932 --> 28:06.393
You still have feelings for him.
I see it in your eyes.

28:06.476 --> 28:08.520
[somber music]

28:14.943 --> 28:15.944
Han Ki-jun.

28:16.027 --> 28:17.112
I'm so happy for you

28:17.195 --> 28:19.489
and I need you to leave
my relationships alone.

28:19.572 --> 28:22.283
I know that I did you wrong
when I was your boyfriend,

28:22.784 --> 28:24.994
so I want to do right by you
as a friend, Ha-kyung.

28:26.329 --> 28:28.790
I'm only saying this,
'cause I'm worried about you

28:28.873 --> 28:30.458
as a friend, please.

28:31.501 --> 28:32.919
Don't just say goodbye.

28:35.422 --> 28:37.090
And I don't say it for his sake,

28:38.216 --> 28:39.217
I say it for yours.

28:41.136 --> 28:42.429
I've learned not to

28:43.763 --> 28:46.474
let the good ones get away anymore,
trust me, Ha-kyung.

28:52.063 --> 28:55.608
MOTEL
KARAOKE

29:03.783 --> 29:06.035
[tense music]

29:10.415 --> 29:11.416
[sighs]

29:11.499 --> 29:14.043
IMI MOTEL

29:14.127 --> 29:15.253
[sighs]

29:16.588 --> 29:17.839
[restaurant owner] Let me think.

29:19.048 --> 29:21.259
Was he here? No, no, not today.

29:22.802 --> 29:25.722
- Thank you.
- [restaurant owner] Sure. Good luck.

29:25.805 --> 29:28.558
[indistinct chatter]

29:28.641 --> 29:29.517
[man] Hey.

29:29.601 --> 29:31.019
Sorry to bother you.

29:32.187 --> 29:35.190
- [bells clinking]
- [overlapping chatter]

29:39.152 --> 29:41.362
[pants]

29:43.865 --> 29:45.450
- What? Family leave?
- [Dong-han] Yeah.

29:45.533 --> 29:47.869
He didn't say what,
but, yeah, family thing.

29:48.495 --> 29:50.455
He wanted me to let you know
that he's off.

29:51.289 --> 29:53.583
He called Team One
and asked their Severe Weather Forecaster

29:53.666 --> 29:55.126
to come in early and cover him.

29:56.127 --> 29:57.253
Then he ran off.

29:57.337 --> 30:00.298
You don't know what's going on
with him, do you?

30:00.381 --> 30:02.383
[tense music]

30:11.768 --> 30:14.854
[nurse] It looks like Mr. Lee Myung-han
left the hospital this morning.

30:14.938 --> 30:17.649
What? But I thought there was more to do?
What did he say?

30:17.732 --> 30:19.943
We reached out to his son
shortly after he left.

30:20.527 --> 30:21.861
Perhaps he knew.

30:23.613 --> 30:25.532
Right, thank you. I'll give him a call.

30:26.699 --> 30:27.534
[beeps]

30:32.288 --> 30:34.290
[background chatter]

30:49.597 --> 30:51.933
[operator] The person you are
trying to reach is unavailable.

30:52.016 --> 30:56.229
You will be connected to voicemail.
Please leave a message after the tone.

31:00.233 --> 31:01.150
[sighs]

31:05.613 --> 31:06.781
Ugh!

31:06.865 --> 31:10.076
The price of that napa cabbage.
Just when I think it can't get higher.

31:10.702 --> 31:13.037
- It's not worth it anymore. You can't…
- [bus steam hissing]

31:13.121 --> 31:14.831
Oh, no. Oh, no. That's my bus, isn't it?

31:26.634 --> 31:27.719
It can't be.

31:34.225 --> 31:36.185
FATHER

31:36.269 --> 31:38.271
[cell phone buzzing]

31:40.565 --> 31:41.733
Hey, Dad.

31:43.818 --> 31:45.528
Dad, where did you go off to?

31:46.237 --> 31:47.989
I said where did you go?

31:49.157 --> 31:50.241
[sighs]

31:50.325 --> 31:52.619
[mellow music]

31:52.702 --> 31:55.705
Ugh, kid, relax,
I'll go deaf listening to that.

31:58.166 --> 31:59.584
Where are you right now?

31:59.667 --> 32:01.794
That's none of your business, kid.

32:03.129 --> 32:04.422
Then what did you call for?

32:04.505 --> 32:06.257
Because I've got something to say to you.

32:08.384 --> 32:12.180
Every time I think about it,
I think you should get her back.

32:14.098 --> 32:15.934
You gotta stop being so stubborn.

32:17.435 --> 32:18.728
You can't let her slip away.

32:18.811 --> 32:19.896
Got it?

32:20.605 --> 32:21.814
You should not.

32:21.898 --> 32:24.901
You'll never gonna find another like her.
Do you understand?

32:27.028 --> 32:30.365
You got screwed over when it comes to Dad.
It's tough luck.

32:31.449 --> 32:32.617
But you got her.

32:32.700 --> 32:34.702
[mellow music]

32:36.079 --> 32:37.080
Hey, Dad.

32:38.289 --> 32:39.457
Where are you?

32:39.540 --> 32:42.585
You know they had more tests to do,
and the doctors said…

32:43.211 --> 32:46.130
depending on the test results,
they'll wanna do surgery.

32:46.214 --> 32:47.674
If you start chemo now--

32:47.757 --> 32:49.634
[Myung-han] Oh, we don't need
to talk about that.

32:50.593 --> 32:52.345
It's not like I deserve your concern.

32:52.428 --> 32:54.138
So what?

32:55.765 --> 32:58.559
You still have time to be a good father
before you go.

33:01.813 --> 33:03.606
If you care about me at all,

33:03.690 --> 33:06.442
you'd leave me
with at least one good memory.

33:07.652 --> 33:09.028
'Cause I care, either way.

33:09.612 --> 33:12.740
I'm going to do everything I can
to help you, and after that,

33:13.533 --> 33:15.910
I won't cry, even if you die,
I'll stop bothering you.

33:16.577 --> 33:17.745
So, please.

33:19.288 --> 33:20.790
Get the treatment.

33:24.168 --> 33:25.795
Stay with me that long.

33:27.880 --> 33:29.340
Just until then,

33:30.133 --> 33:33.469
I want you to be like a real father.

33:35.638 --> 33:36.681
Come on, kid.

33:38.391 --> 33:40.309
Just say you want me to die.

33:42.228 --> 33:44.731
Please.
[sobbing]

33:44.814 --> 33:46.858
["Love Hurts A Little More"
by Kim Na-young playing]

33:53.990 --> 33:55.074
Shit.

33:57.535 --> 33:58.870
[sniffles]

34:00.538 --> 34:01.622
Hey, kid.

34:02.206 --> 34:05.376
I know you think I'm dirt,
but I'm not all that.

34:07.253 --> 34:10.631
I care about you, I do.
Don't think I don't.

34:11.716 --> 34:13.009
All right, Dad.

34:15.845 --> 34:18.681
Nevermind.
We don't have to talk about that.

34:19.390 --> 34:21.392
I want you to get your girl back.

34:22.101 --> 34:23.102
[exhales heavily]

34:24.145 --> 34:26.147
Consider it my last wish.

34:26.230 --> 34:28.232
["Love Hurts A Little More"
by Kim Na-young playing]

34:38.868 --> 34:41.537
[sobbing]

34:45.500 --> 34:46.667
I'd get better, too.

34:46.751 --> 34:48.044
[Si-woo] He has lung cancer.

34:49.712 --> 34:51.923
They'd like to run more tests tomorrow.

34:52.006 --> 34:55.510
If you still have to take him in,
do what you have to do.

35:01.766 --> 35:03.893
["Love Hurts A Little More"
by Kim Na-young playing]

35:13.277 --> 35:14.320
Sorry.

35:30.878 --> 35:31.796
[sighs]

35:44.308 --> 35:46.644
[operator] The person you are
trying to reach is unavailable.

35:46.727 --> 35:48.604
Please leave a message after the tone.

35:48.688 --> 35:51.274
[sobbing]

35:52.108 --> 35:54.110
[somber music]

36:17.592 --> 36:19.010
[clears throat, sniffles]

36:25.141 --> 36:26.225
[clears throat]

36:27.560 --> 36:29.478
What's wrong, Tae-kyung?

36:30.146 --> 36:32.940
You wanted me to come and meet you?

36:34.942 --> 36:36.485
You've got a whole bottle.

36:42.783 --> 36:43.659
What's wrong?

36:44.702 --> 36:46.245
They said they won't do it.

36:47.997 --> 36:49.498
What are you talking about? Who?

36:50.333 --> 36:51.751
That publisher.

36:52.376 --> 36:54.462
They said my story is no good.

36:54.545 --> 36:56.339
That they can't publish it.

36:56.422 --> 36:57.340
Oh.

36:58.049 --> 36:59.675
But why?

37:00.218 --> 37:02.303
Why not? What did they say, huh?

37:02.386 --> 37:03.387
What's the reasoning?

37:04.680 --> 37:06.390
They agree with what you said.

37:07.099 --> 37:08.392
They what?

37:08.476 --> 37:11.437
What… What did they say exactly?

37:11.520 --> 37:13.731
It didn't have a hook.
[chuckles]

37:15.733 --> 37:16.776
[exhales deeply]

37:16.859 --> 37:19.737
Anything for kids without a hook,

37:19.820 --> 37:23.491
won't stand a chance competing
with everything else.

37:28.996 --> 37:30.081
So that's it.

37:31.374 --> 37:32.833
I'm through.

37:34.085 --> 37:36.212
- You're through?
- [chuckles]

37:37.255 --> 37:40.466
- Writing. Never again.
- You can't. That's ridiculous.

37:40.549 --> 37:42.927
It's not like
they're the only publishers in Korea.

37:43.511 --> 37:45.471
Yeah. It is, though.

37:46.097 --> 37:48.015
I tried everywhere else.

37:48.099 --> 37:52.270
They were the only ones
interested in working with me.

37:52.353 --> 37:54.855
I managed to ruin that too, so…

37:54.939 --> 37:56.816
[chuckles]

37:56.899 --> 37:59.151
Why are they all so… It's not--

38:00.611 --> 38:02.446
Oh, jeez.

38:02.530 --> 38:04.407
You can't seriously quit.

38:05.866 --> 38:08.286
Look, Seok-ho, I'm sorry.

38:08.369 --> 38:11.914
This is just what happens
to people like me.

38:12.915 --> 38:14.625
I don't have a hook.

38:15.668 --> 38:17.545
Even with my mom.

38:17.628 --> 38:21.674
That's the reason my ex-husband left, too.

38:23.050 --> 38:25.094
Listen, you don't need
a hook for me, okay?

38:25.803 --> 38:28.681
- I swear I'll never--
- You will, eventually.

38:31.017 --> 38:33.477
[sniffs]
I start okay, then get boring.

38:34.353 --> 38:36.105
I've always been that way.

38:37.940 --> 38:38.774
[sighs]

38:39.608 --> 38:43.779
Then it'll hurt a lot
when we break up like the rest.

38:43.863 --> 38:46.115
[mellow music]

38:50.494 --> 38:53.873
You think we're doomed?
What are you saying right now?

38:57.585 --> 38:58.461
[inhales sharply]

39:03.466 --> 39:04.800
Let's get it over with.

39:12.183 --> 39:14.310
[mellow music]

39:42.922 --> 39:44.924
Here. You can sit.

39:54.100 --> 39:55.059
Oh.

39:57.812 --> 40:00.189
You left so you can live like this?

40:01.982 --> 40:03.359
Why did you come all the way here?

40:06.987 --> 40:10.825
Here's some clean underwear and socks,
there are some shirts, too.

40:13.452 --> 40:15.371
Also, you're horrible, you know that?

40:16.288 --> 40:17.540
No, you're not.

40:17.623 --> 40:19.417
You're not horrible, just stupid.

40:21.502 --> 40:22.837
What are you talking about?

40:22.920 --> 40:25.256
You were the one that wanted to wait.

40:25.339 --> 40:27.842
"Just give me three months,"
that's what you said, Dong-han.

40:27.925 --> 40:29.301
And now you want out.

40:29.385 --> 40:32.805
After less than a month of trying,
you gave up and signed.

40:32.888 --> 40:35.516
If you really weren't going to try,
you shouldn't have led us on

40:35.599 --> 40:37.226
like you wanted to keep us together.

40:38.102 --> 40:41.772
I'll never be good enough for you,
no matter how much I want to.

40:43.232 --> 40:45.526
Once I realized that,
I thought I shouldn't drag things out.

40:46.485 --> 40:47.695
So I signed the papers.

40:47.778 --> 40:49.238
You don't want to commit.

40:50.739 --> 40:54.118
I did commit.
In the entirety of our marriage,

40:54.201 --> 40:56.245
I've been faithful to you as a husband.

40:56.328 --> 40:57.872
We were never your first love.

40:57.955 --> 40:59.999
- That's because you two--
- [Hyang-rae] Okay.

41:00.082 --> 41:02.460
You caught me
and you called my bluff. Well done.

41:02.543 --> 41:04.503
I thought divorce papers
would scare you straight

41:04.587 --> 41:05.421
and you'd step up.

41:05.504 --> 41:07.548
I can't believe you just signed it.

41:08.215 --> 41:09.925
A real man doesn't give up.

41:10.009 --> 41:13.095
What does that say about me
who's just been waiting for you?

41:13.179 --> 41:15.139
And I don't know how you can look Bo-mi
in the eyes

41:15.222 --> 41:16.974
now that she's finally been
opening up to you.

41:17.558 --> 41:19.101
If you don't care enough to keep trying,

41:19.185 --> 41:21.687
why did you lead us on
like you were coming home finally, huh?

41:24.231 --> 41:25.691
Tell Bo-mi yourself.

41:26.984 --> 41:30.321
You can give up on us, but Bo-mi?

41:30.404 --> 41:31.655
[sighs]

41:35.993 --> 41:39.497
You're a complete coward.
Do you know that? You are!

41:40.372 --> 41:42.291
Hyang-rae, I… I thought--

41:42.374 --> 41:44.585
Are you so clever
you can guess the weather,

41:44.668 --> 41:47.046
yet have no idea how your family is doing?

41:47.129 --> 41:48.380
Sorry.

41:49.048 --> 41:51.050
I'm really sorry, Hyang-rae.

41:51.133 --> 41:54.470
Enough. I'm sick of hearing you say
how sorry you are.

41:55.262 --> 41:57.848
What else can I possibly say?

41:57.932 --> 42:01.310
What's left? There's nothing for me to say
other than that I'm sorry.

42:01.894 --> 42:02.853
Try "thank you."

42:05.648 --> 42:07.691
"Thank you for waiting so long."

42:07.775 --> 42:09.735
"You were patient, thank you."

42:09.818 --> 42:12.738
You're so busy you can't eat
with your daughter on her birthday.

42:13.906 --> 42:17.201
She was so excited
that you even made a reservation.

42:17.284 --> 42:18.702
You tell her, "Thank you."

42:20.287 --> 42:21.705
[sobs]

42:23.958 --> 42:26.001
Why are you so thickhead?

42:26.085 --> 42:28.045
Why are you so unaware?

42:28.879 --> 42:30.881
[dramatic music]

42:32.299 --> 42:33.300
[Dong-han] I'm sorry.

42:34.093 --> 42:35.344
I'm sorry.

42:38.639 --> 42:39.598
I'm sorry.

42:41.559 --> 42:42.726
Thank you, Hyang-rae.

42:45.980 --> 42:48.065
Thank you for everything.

42:48.649 --> 42:49.692
Thank you.

42:56.699 --> 42:58.826
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

43:02.871 --> 43:04.832
- Director, I have the results here.
- Okay.

43:06.667 --> 43:09.420
As expected,
there's a possibility we'll see 5mm

43:09.503 --> 43:11.297
of rain early tomorrow.

43:11.380 --> 43:13.215
I'll add that to the weekend forecast.

43:13.299 --> 43:15.342
- Yeah. Okay.
- Excuse me.

43:16.051 --> 43:18.804
We think the temperature
will drop to 3 degrees by then.

43:18.887 --> 43:19.763
It might not rain.

43:20.973 --> 43:22.391
[Si-woo] With the current data,

43:22.474 --> 43:27.187
there's more than a 50 percent chance
the temperature will drop to one degree.

43:27.271 --> 43:30.107
That would mean, there's
an 80 percent chance of snow instead.

43:30.190 --> 43:31.400
That's what I was thinking.

43:31.483 --> 43:32.776
He's not wrong.

43:34.945 --> 43:36.989
We could recheck the precipitation data

43:37.072 --> 43:39.992
and do an analysis of the snowfall's
liquid water equivalent?

43:40.075 --> 43:41.285
How long will that take?

43:41.368 --> 43:42.953
Less than an hour, I'd say.

43:43.579 --> 43:45.706
- Let's get it started.
- Okay.

43:47.333 --> 43:49.585
[trainees gasping]

43:54.757 --> 43:56.258
[trainee 1] She's so cool.

44:00.346 --> 44:01.680
Oh, is that so?

44:02.765 --> 44:03.849
Yes, all right.

44:06.352 --> 44:08.854
What is it? What did they say?

44:09.438 --> 44:11.357
The precipitation forecast for the weekend

44:11.440 --> 44:13.192
could actually be for snow, but we'll see.

44:13.942 --> 44:15.944
- We should prepare.
- [woman sighs]

44:16.028 --> 44:18.364
Oh, I got a bad feeling about this.

44:22.117 --> 44:23.077
Jeez.

44:23.786 --> 44:27.665
It could be snow or rain,
and the odds are split in half?

44:27.748 --> 44:29.041
[Dong-han] Yes.

44:29.124 --> 44:30.876
[Bong-chan] Mm. Oh, jeez.

44:30.959 --> 44:33.879
Last time this happened,
wasn't it a huge mess?

44:33.962 --> 44:37.216
Yes. December of 2001,
the same thing happened,

44:37.299 --> 44:39.760
and we forecasted heavy snow
during evening rush hour.

44:39.843 --> 44:42.388
It wound up not getting cold enough,
so we just got rain.

44:42.471 --> 44:46.517
Criticism was so intense we had to undergo
a federal investigation.

44:47.101 --> 44:48.769
[clicks tongue]
Okay, listen up.

44:49.269 --> 44:51.772
If it does turn into snow,
it's the first snow of the year.

44:52.356 --> 44:54.900
Right? That means the public and the press

44:54.983 --> 44:56.318
will watch us especially closely.

44:56.402 --> 44:57.277
[all] Yes.

44:57.361 --> 44:58.570
Um, excuse me.

44:59.154 --> 45:00.322
It snowed already.

45:00.406 --> 45:02.658
The day before yesterday,
I saw it early in the morning.

45:02.741 --> 45:04.493
[trainee 2] It definitely snowed
in my neighborhood.

45:04.576 --> 45:05.994
It snowed in my neighborhood, too.

45:06.078 --> 45:09.039
Yeah, uh, can someone explain it to him?

45:09.832 --> 45:10.999
- Miss Kim?
- [Soo-jin] Yes?

45:11.083 --> 45:13.460
Can you share what we mean
by the "first snow"?

45:13.544 --> 45:14.461
Oh.

45:15.879 --> 45:16.755
Okay.

45:19.383 --> 45:22.094
The official first snow
has specific criteria.

45:22.177 --> 45:24.054
We use this
for any special meteorological event,

45:24.138 --> 45:26.306
and apply them to data
from all over the country.

45:26.390 --> 45:29.101
For example, we would need someone
from the Seoul Observatory

45:29.184 --> 45:32.521
to see the snow, and then check
that it hits all the criteria

45:32.604 --> 45:34.314
to declare Seoul's first snow.

45:35.232 --> 45:37.526
Do you understand? Does that make sense?

45:37.609 --> 45:39.069
[trainees] Yes.

45:39.153 --> 45:41.738
- [Soo-jin chuckles]
- Wow, Team Two is so cool.

45:41.822 --> 45:44.116
[trainee 2]
Man, I hope I get to work at HQ.

45:44.199 --> 45:47.244
[trainee 3] Nah, they said only the best
of the best get in here.

45:47.327 --> 45:49.955
We're all set?
Huh, enough training for today.

45:50.038 --> 45:52.833
Hm? Back to the meeting.
[sniffs]

45:52.916 --> 45:55.711
Director Jin, your final thoughts?

45:57.045 --> 45:58.714
It's absolutely going to snow.

45:59.673 --> 46:02.134
If we put the relative humidity
at 80 percent,

46:02.217 --> 46:03.760
and the temperature is 3 degrees,

46:04.344 --> 46:07.222
there's less than a 20 percent chance
it will become snow.

46:07.306 --> 46:08.891
But if the temperature goes
down one degree,

46:08.974 --> 46:11.059
then we're at a 77 percent chance.

46:11.143 --> 46:14.980
And with the way things are now,
the odds that the temperature will drop

46:15.063 --> 46:18.442
to one degree Celsius in the next two days
is at 50 percent.

46:18.525 --> 46:20.569
True, but the temperature rose
to 6 degrees today

46:20.652 --> 46:22.613
even though it's been below zero for days.

46:22.696 --> 46:24.072
You all know that.

46:24.156 --> 46:26.700
Yes, but the air has changed drastically
since midnight yesterday.

46:26.783 --> 46:28.952
So we have less than a 50 percent chance

46:29.036 --> 46:30.787
that the temperature
will fall this evening.

46:31.580 --> 46:34.041
Can't you see how unstable
the atmosphere is now?

46:34.124 --> 46:37.044
When the sun goes down, the air
temperature will fall exponentially.

46:37.127 --> 46:39.421
[pensive music]

46:41.215 --> 46:43.926
Here's that analysis
you requested earlier.

46:47.471 --> 46:49.139
LIQUID WATER EQUIVALENT ANALYSIS

46:54.770 --> 46:55.896
[Bong-chan] So…

46:56.480 --> 46:57.648
Director Jin.

46:59.358 --> 47:00.484
What's your call?

47:06.490 --> 47:08.408
[Ha-kyung] I wish you just tell me, sir.

47:08.492 --> 47:09.451
What?

47:09.535 --> 47:13.163
Who has the least accurate forecast
at the KMA?

47:15.290 --> 47:16.917
Oh, what?
[laughs]

47:17.543 --> 47:19.419
It's been ages,
you haven't put it together?

47:19.503 --> 47:21.463
I haven't and I'd really like to know.

47:21.547 --> 47:23.382
What's your secret?

47:23.465 --> 47:26.009
Your forecast are consistently right
with detailed accuracy.

47:26.093 --> 47:30.055
And I looked, they don't have records
of who got what wrong.

47:30.138 --> 47:31.348
[chuckles]

47:31.431 --> 47:33.225
Of course, they don't. Why would they?

47:34.726 --> 47:36.395
Want me to tell you who it is?

47:36.478 --> 47:38.647
Yes. I'd really like to know
if you're willing to share.

47:39.231 --> 47:40.065
Hm…

47:41.733 --> 47:43.777
- I am.
- What?

47:44.570 --> 47:45.404
Yeah.

47:45.487 --> 47:49.366
Oh! You can't have…
You can't be the best and the worst.

47:50.701 --> 47:52.327
I am, though, so…

47:53.662 --> 47:54.746
Hm…

47:55.664 --> 47:59.418
Over the years,
I found that getting it wrong,

48:00.002 --> 48:03.630
can often teach you more than
if you got it right the first time around.

48:06.008 --> 48:09.177
So if you learn something each instance
that you got it wrong,

48:09.261 --> 48:11.388
then one day, you'll figure it out.

48:11.972 --> 48:15.434
And your accuracy rate
goes way up over time.

48:16.852 --> 48:17.769
Makes sense?

48:18.270 --> 48:21.773
So the secret
to my record-breaking accuracy rate

48:21.857 --> 48:25.235
is simply not to focus
on how to get it right.

48:25.777 --> 48:28.071
You have to learn how not to get it wrong.

48:28.155 --> 48:29.197
[sighs]

48:30.532 --> 48:33.452
Wasn't it hard getting it wrong again
so many times?

48:34.036 --> 48:36.997
It was. But no one else
keeps track of that.

48:38.749 --> 48:40.208
So how do you stop caring?

48:41.501 --> 48:43.670
You don't. You have to keep going on.

48:44.921 --> 48:47.591
I held myself accountable
for each call I made.

48:48.425 --> 48:50.552
And I knew I worked harder
than anyone else did

48:51.178 --> 48:54.097
in the hours I was deciding
those forecasts.

48:58.268 --> 48:59.353
Director Jin.

48:59.853 --> 49:01.855
What will you say in the forecast?

49:01.938 --> 49:04.066
[tense music]

49:10.322 --> 49:12.407
Considering the data,
here are my thoughts.

49:12.491 --> 49:15.118
We're expecting snow after midnight.

49:15.202 --> 49:18.538
The snow will start in the west,
including the Seoul metropolitan areas.

49:18.622 --> 49:21.833
We're expecting 3 to 5cm of snow
in the central region.

49:21.917 --> 49:25.712
Oh. Can you believe the work it took
to get those three lines?

49:26.463 --> 49:28.507
It really was totally worth it.

49:30.592 --> 49:33.303
So, when are they going to transfer you?

49:35.180 --> 49:37.933
I don't know yet. Not for a while, though.

49:39.434 --> 49:40.686
What?

49:40.769 --> 49:42.688
I thought you were leaving us soon.

49:43.563 --> 49:45.691
It was looking like that
for a little while.

49:45.774 --> 49:47.734
It'd just be a waste, I thought.

49:47.818 --> 49:49.903
All the time and hard work
I put in with you,

49:49.986 --> 49:55.659
- I can't just throw that all away.
- So you're staying with us on Team Two?

49:56.201 --> 49:59.496
And I thought it was so nice
how the newbies looked up to me like that.

49:59.579 --> 50:01.915
They said HQs were the best of the best.

50:01.998 --> 50:03.417
[chuckles]

50:04.292 --> 50:07.754
So I'm sticking around,
at least until one of the newbies

50:07.838 --> 50:08.880
is worthy of us.

50:08.964 --> 50:14.136
Oh! You look so cute.
Look at you, that's great!

50:15.053 --> 50:19.182
Oh, I'm torn between shouting hooray
and calling you an idiot.

50:19.266 --> 50:21.184
Oh, tell me it was the right thing to do.

50:21.268 --> 50:22.602
Come on.

50:23.353 --> 50:25.021
Okay. I'm buying you dinner.

50:25.105 --> 50:26.398
[gasps]
What about barbecue?

50:27.941 --> 50:29.735
- I'll cover two rounds, okay?
- Yay!

50:29.818 --> 50:30.736
[both laugh]

50:30.819 --> 50:32.279
Oh, we can walk.

50:33.530 --> 50:37.075
[indistinct chatter]

50:45.250 --> 50:47.085
[automated voice] Doors closing.

51:11.067 --> 51:12.527
Guess it's not here yet.

51:13.278 --> 51:14.112
No.

51:15.655 --> 51:16.990
Was this your first one?

51:17.949 --> 51:18.992
Huh?

51:20.452 --> 51:21.703
Your first snow warning.

51:22.996 --> 51:24.664
Oh, yes.

51:25.832 --> 51:29.252
Mm, it's the hardest one
to call, isn't it?

51:30.128 --> 51:31.671
- Yeah.
- [chuckles]

51:34.466 --> 51:35.467
What did I say?

51:35.550 --> 51:37.928
It's just, last time,
you said localized heavy rain

51:38.011 --> 51:39.513
was the toughest forecast.

51:40.806 --> 51:45.060
Did I? Well, I'd say
it's hard if it falls from the sky.

51:45.143 --> 51:47.646
- Right?
- True.

51:48.438 --> 51:50.690
You did well. Keep going.

51:51.358 --> 51:52.442
Have a good night.

51:53.610 --> 51:55.612
[mellow music]

52:26.268 --> 52:28.144
[chuckles]

52:28.228 --> 52:30.146
[squeals]
I'm sorry.

52:30.230 --> 52:32.482
I was craving grapefruit so much.

52:33.024 --> 52:34.860
- Was it cold?
- No, it was fine.

52:34.943 --> 52:36.653
- Drink up, okay?
- Mm.

52:40.198 --> 52:41.283
How is it?

52:41.825 --> 52:43.326
Mmm!

52:44.035 --> 52:46.288
- It's so good. I feel better.
- [laughs]

52:46.371 --> 52:48.707
Told you. They said eat what you want.

52:49.291 --> 52:51.251
It should comfort
the morning sickness as well.

52:51.334 --> 52:52.627
[chuckles]

52:52.711 --> 52:54.379
Did you get that from a mommy group?

52:54.963 --> 52:56.006
Mm-hm, of course.

52:56.089 --> 52:59.134
I asked them a question online,
and they invited me right in.

52:59.217 --> 53:01.052
It's really super informative.

53:01.136 --> 53:02.888
[both chuckle]

53:02.971 --> 53:03.972
Oh no.

53:04.055 --> 53:05.682
Who's this old lady? Where's my husband?

53:05.765 --> 53:06.892
I'd be a great old lady.

53:06.975 --> 53:09.477
- Any other cravings?
- I'm set.

53:09.561 --> 53:11.021
Okay. Should we go?

53:15.025 --> 53:16.943
Is it gonna snow in the morning?

53:17.027 --> 53:18.445
The sky is clear right now.

53:19.112 --> 53:20.697
Mm, it does.

53:20.780 --> 53:23.158
If it does, it'll be rough.

53:23.241 --> 53:25.243
If it doesn't, then we're wrong,
it's rough, too.

53:25.327 --> 53:28.455
If I got to say, it'll snow a whole lot.

53:28.538 --> 53:31.416
And everything will be covered
in white tomorrow.

53:31.499 --> 53:33.335
[both chuckle]

53:33.418 --> 53:35.128
[automated voice] Doors opening.

53:36.880 --> 53:37.714
Mother!

53:37.797 --> 53:40.383
- [automated voice] Doors closing.
- What are you doing here? It's so cold.

53:40.467 --> 53:42.719
Well, my daughter changed
the damn door code,

53:42.802 --> 53:44.429
so I couldn't get in.
What else could I do?

53:44.512 --> 53:47.265
Sure, I could get hypothermia,
but what else can I do?

53:47.349 --> 53:48.308
[groans]

53:48.391 --> 53:51.478
- [Mrs. Bae] My legs.
- You're seriously insane.

53:52.562 --> 53:54.314
[door lock chimes]

53:54.397 --> 53:55.899
[Ha-kyung] Go on. Get inside.

54:17.587 --> 54:18.713
Drink this.

54:19.214 --> 54:20.882
Are you still cold?

54:23.593 --> 54:25.261
Yeah, I was frozen solid waiting for you.

54:25.345 --> 54:27.013
Are you happy now?

54:29.933 --> 54:33.853
I don't know why you keep coming over
when you know I might not be here.

54:33.937 --> 54:38.066
And stop bringing me food, too.
I almost always have to eat out.

54:39.526 --> 54:40.652
It's Si-woo again.

54:42.320 --> 54:43.613
Lee Si-woo? What did you do?

54:43.697 --> 54:45.240
Did you see him again?

54:45.323 --> 54:47.575
I heard his dad's not doing well?

54:52.580 --> 54:53.957
Si-woo said that to you?

54:55.375 --> 54:56.376
[sighs]

54:56.459 --> 54:58.503
That's why he called it off, I think.

54:58.586 --> 54:59.713
To protect you.

55:03.633 --> 55:09.305
You know, that man, he's very young.
It must be very difficult.

55:11.558 --> 55:14.352
Lee Si-woo says his dad
has always made his life harder.

55:15.145 --> 55:16.062
[clicks tongue]

55:16.563 --> 55:20.316
Ah, you know better than to see an elder
as any kind of burden.

55:20.400 --> 55:22.152
That's what he is, though.

55:22.235 --> 55:24.821
You have no idea how much
he's held Si-woo back.

55:25.405 --> 55:28.283
Getting him legal trouble,
asking his son for a loan.

55:30.076 --> 55:34.539
So, you don't want to stay
with him, 'cause of that?

55:35.123 --> 55:36.332
Is it too risky?

55:37.500 --> 55:39.085
I never said I didn't want to stay.

55:39.169 --> 55:40.712
Then it works out.

55:40.795 --> 55:44.215
Your door code's even the man's birthday
for crying out loud.

55:44.758 --> 55:47.427
The door code isn't his birthday.

55:47.510 --> 55:49.512
I saw it. Don't lie to me again.

55:49.596 --> 55:51.681
Zero, three, one, four.

55:51.765 --> 55:54.476
It's not my birthday,
it's not Tae-kyung's, and it's not yours,

55:54.559 --> 55:56.770
it's not your father's, either.

55:56.853 --> 55:59.022
It's got to be his birthday, so…

56:01.024 --> 56:02.358
Don't you know the date and hour?

56:02.942 --> 56:04.736
I'm telling you the truth.

56:05.445 --> 56:07.655
Okay, ha, maybe you are compatible.

56:07.739 --> 56:09.824
I give up if you really won't admit it.

56:09.908 --> 56:11.785
It's another date.

56:13.078 --> 56:14.621
It's when we first saw each other.

56:15.288 --> 56:16.706
March 14th.

56:19.417 --> 56:22.754
We hadn't met before that,
Lee Si-woo and I.

56:25.256 --> 56:26.508
[chuckles softly]

56:28.176 --> 56:31.054
If that's what you chose
for your door code,

56:31.137 --> 56:32.972
why aren't you two together?

56:39.687 --> 56:41.689
[melancholy music]

56:41.773 --> 56:42.607
'Cause…

56:43.817 --> 56:45.610
you can't stay together…

56:48.238 --> 56:50.115
only to avoid breaking up.

56:50.907 --> 56:52.909
He's the one that wanted it. I can't…

56:53.701 --> 56:55.870
What can I do, get on my knees and beg?

56:57.122 --> 56:58.498
And I'm his boss.

56:59.749 --> 57:01.376
It is too risky.

57:07.215 --> 57:08.341
Honestly…

57:09.050 --> 57:13.012
[sobbing]
I've been so sad, Mama.

57:15.265 --> 57:17.559
[melancholy music]

57:32.115 --> 57:33.992
[exhales deeply]

57:35.410 --> 57:38.663
Want to know how ridiculous
this sounds to an outsider?

57:39.164 --> 57:40.999
"It's over 'cause we're in love."

57:41.875 --> 57:46.254
I mean, that's the dumbest most
paradoxical thing I've ever heard.

57:46.337 --> 57:48.214
It should end 'cause you're in love?

57:48.298 --> 57:50.341
What's the sense in you two breaking up?

57:50.425 --> 57:51.384
Is there any?

57:52.927 --> 57:54.804
With that, if you stay broken up,

57:55.430 --> 57:57.932
then you really
just don't love her at all.

58:02.604 --> 58:03.521
I do, though.

58:03.605 --> 58:05.690
She said the break was your idea first.

58:06.316 --> 58:07.775
It was.

58:07.859 --> 58:10.653
Only because I didn't want
to hurt at all, so…

58:10.737 --> 58:12.822
Come on. You said it first.

58:15.992 --> 58:19.412
I didn't think that she
would go for it right away.

58:19.496 --> 58:21.206
I said, "Yeah, let's break up."

58:21.873 --> 58:24.709
In reality, I'm disappointed and…

58:25.877 --> 58:27.295
really upset.

58:27.378 --> 58:31.090
Then you should've told her
you changed your mind. Why not tell her?

58:34.177 --> 58:37.514
'Cause she might have been wanting
to break up, anyway.

58:38.681 --> 58:40.600
She probably had her own reasons.

58:40.683 --> 58:42.227
Like, she could have thought,

58:43.937 --> 58:45.063
I'm too much.

58:45.813 --> 58:47.065
Oh, no.

58:47.774 --> 58:51.778
Life is far too short,
even if you're young, huh.

58:56.908 --> 58:58.117
What are you saying?

58:58.660 --> 59:01.496
Don't get caught up
worrying about the weather tomorrow.

59:01.579 --> 59:03.957
'Cause you can miss how things are today.

59:04.624 --> 59:06.459
Take a second to look up at the sky.

59:06.543 --> 59:08.753
Go to the roof, just to feel the wind.

59:08.836 --> 59:11.214
Look into the eyes of someone
that really loves you.

59:12.048 --> 59:14.050
If you can't make the most
of the current day,

59:14.133 --> 59:16.678
you don't deserve to be
worrying about tomorrow.

59:16.761 --> 59:18.972
That's why you miss things
and get it wrong.

59:19.847 --> 59:20.932
Mama.

59:23.518 --> 59:25.603
Life is short, I know.

59:25.687 --> 59:29.357
Life is like a cloud that shoots
across the sky on a windy day.

59:29.941 --> 59:31.442
Do you follow, smarty-pants?

59:32.944 --> 59:33.945
[Mrs. Bae sighs]

59:36.155 --> 59:38.700
- I'm going home.
- You're going?

59:39.284 --> 59:41.202
Don't walk me out. It's cold.

59:45.498 --> 59:46.499
[door opens]

59:49.252 --> 59:50.253
[door closes]

59:51.879 --> 59:53.047
[sighs]

01:00:04.183 --> 01:00:06.394
[somber music]

01:00:10.398 --> 01:00:12.191
[Ha-kyung] "You shine brightly
when you tell me

01:00:12.275 --> 01:00:15.903
that rain needs to meet another rain
for them to get drenched."

01:00:16.946 --> 01:00:19.198
- Let it rain.
- What was that?

01:00:20.450 --> 01:00:23.161
["Promise You" by Kyuhyun playing]

01:00:48.770 --> 01:00:51.731
Ugh, I'll never date
a co-worker ever again.

01:00:52.315 --> 01:00:54.817
[Si-woo] Really? "Never" is a strong word.

01:00:55.360 --> 01:00:59.656
[Ha-kyung] I know. I'm never going to date
anyone I work with, never again.

01:01:02.659 --> 01:01:07.246
[Ha-kyung] But I did. I embarked
on that path again knowing the cost.

01:01:13.378 --> 01:01:14.921
Why did I do that?

01:01:15.755 --> 01:01:17.757
["Promise You" by Kyuhyun playing]

01:01:25.723 --> 01:01:26.974
[sighs]

01:01:29.936 --> 01:01:32.939
[indistinct chatter]

01:01:52.041 --> 01:01:54.961
I like you more than anyone I've known.

01:01:58.047 --> 01:02:00.675
["Promise You" by Kyuhyun playing]

01:02:25.742 --> 01:02:27.160
Forecaster Lee Si-woo, you…

01:02:29.495 --> 01:02:30.621
[Si-woo] Jin Ha-kyung,

01:02:31.706 --> 01:02:33.040
it's always been you.

01:02:39.797 --> 01:02:40.965
[Ha-kyung] Lee Si-woo.

01:02:41.883 --> 01:02:43.259
It's you.

01:03:02.028 --> 01:03:05.823
- [Si-woo] I just like you, that's all.
- [both chuckle]

01:03:11.829 --> 01:03:13.706
[Ha-kyung] Because I like being with you.

01:03:27.053 --> 01:03:29.055
["Promise You" by Kyuhyun playing]

01:04:05.883 --> 01:04:09.470
I know we forecasted snow,
but that can change any second, right?

01:04:09.554 --> 01:04:11.389
Even if we're just getting rain instead?

01:04:11.472 --> 01:04:13.975
So watch the adiabatic chart's
vertical structure.

01:04:14.058 --> 01:04:15.351
[employees] Okay.

01:04:17.144 --> 01:04:20.398
REAL-TIME RADAR

01:05:14.118 --> 01:05:16.120
[calm music]

01:05:40.102 --> 01:05:43.356
[Si-woo] Told you. See?
It snowed after all.

01:05:44.565 --> 01:05:47.026
["Mind Warning" by Onew playing]

01:05:54.951 --> 01:05:59.246
SEOUL OBSERVATORY

01:06:01.332 --> 01:06:02.792
What are you doing out here?

01:06:04.377 --> 01:06:05.962
I wanted to check the snow.

01:06:07.338 --> 01:06:08.339
[chuckles]

01:06:11.842 --> 01:06:14.720
No one really cares
about the first rain of the year.

01:06:15.429 --> 01:06:17.348
They really love the first snow, though.

01:06:18.599 --> 01:06:19.767
You know?

01:06:20.685 --> 01:06:21.936
You're right.

01:06:23.688 --> 01:06:24.730
[exhales deeply]

01:06:24.814 --> 01:06:28.150
I'll remember this snow for a long while.

01:06:30.236 --> 01:06:33.990
Like how it rained on the day
when I first met you.

01:06:35.241 --> 01:06:36.492
Do you remember?

01:06:37.243 --> 01:06:38.995
The first day we spoke to each other?

01:06:40.079 --> 01:06:43.207
Yeah, "Si-woo," "rain that comes on time."

01:06:44.083 --> 01:06:45.167
Lee Si-woo.

01:06:51.716 --> 01:06:53.718
[raindrops pattering]

01:06:53.801 --> 01:06:55.928
["Mind Warning" by Onew playing]

01:07:05.688 --> 01:07:07.898
- Fourteenth of March.
- [Si-woo] Fourteenth of March.

01:07:09.191 --> 01:07:11.819
[both chuckle]

01:07:13.863 --> 01:07:15.031
You know,

01:07:15.698 --> 01:07:18.284
in Spanish they have the same.

01:07:20.161 --> 01:07:24.081
"Months of sunny days would bring
a drought and then a desert."

01:07:26.667 --> 01:07:28.210
At first, I liked that.

01:07:29.003 --> 01:07:31.964
The Lee Si-woo I knew
is so optimistic and cheerful.

01:07:34.383 --> 01:07:36.927
I was so down those days,
it was a nice change.

01:07:37.970 --> 01:07:40.639
But then, as we got to know each other,

01:07:41.348 --> 01:07:43.225
I saw your pain and learned

01:07:44.268 --> 01:07:46.937
all the things you thought
you had to hide from the world,

01:07:48.105 --> 01:07:51.859
I saw a clear picture of you.

01:07:54.070 --> 01:07:56.030
And I loved you even more for it.

01:08:02.369 --> 01:08:05.998
So I hope you won't be
too hard on yourself

01:08:06.082 --> 01:08:10.044
about that wind and the rain
you've carried with you.

01:08:13.089 --> 01:08:16.300
Wind and rain are meant to pass,
not stay forever.

01:08:19.220 --> 01:08:22.765
Everyone has their own version of a storm.

01:08:23.390 --> 01:08:27.144
And if someone's in it with you,

01:08:27.853 --> 01:08:30.773
waiting with you,
even with the rain and the wind,

01:08:31.982 --> 01:08:34.026
wouldn't you feel like it's all right?

01:08:36.320 --> 01:08:38.823
I'd like the two of us to have that.

01:08:46.747 --> 01:08:51.460
- I don't just flirt around.
- [laughs]

01:08:51.544 --> 01:08:53.379
Well, then it's good
I'm not leading you on.

01:08:55.673 --> 01:08:57.049
So let me date you.

01:08:59.301 --> 01:09:01.262
If we feel something, we date.

01:09:02.263 --> 01:09:03.681
If not, we don't.

01:09:07.977 --> 01:09:09.061
So which is it?

01:09:11.689 --> 01:09:13.983
[romantic music]

01:09:15.693 --> 01:09:16.694
I love you.

01:09:19.947 --> 01:09:22.158
I think I'm really in love. Is that bad?

01:09:24.577 --> 01:09:25.661
[chuckles]

01:09:37.631 --> 01:09:38.549
I love you.

01:09:39.133 --> 01:09:41.135
Just as much. Only more.

01:09:44.346 --> 01:09:46.307
And that love is only gonna grow.

01:09:47.558 --> 01:09:49.143
I'll love you forever.

01:09:54.982 --> 01:09:57.193
[romantic music]

01:10:28.933 --> 01:10:31.185
The snow looks so graceful.

01:10:34.396 --> 01:10:36.815
Think of this
when we're shoveling it tomorrow.

01:10:42.112 --> 01:10:45.157
[cell phone buzzing]

01:10:51.080 --> 01:10:52.373
[exhales deeply]

01:11:00.506 --> 01:11:01.757
[Seok-ho] Tae-kyung.

01:11:01.840 --> 01:11:03.884
[Seok-ho chuckling]

01:11:03.968 --> 01:11:06.762
Uh, I called, because…

01:11:06.845 --> 01:11:08.472
I looked outside,

01:11:10.474 --> 01:11:12.935
the first snow, it's so…

01:11:14.603 --> 01:11:19.400
It just looks…
It's pretty and graceful as it falls.

01:11:19.984 --> 01:11:22.903
It made me think of you.

01:11:27.241 --> 01:11:28.993
I love you so much, Tae-kyung.

01:11:29.076 --> 01:11:31.495
[sobbing]

01:11:32.788 --> 01:11:33.706
I…

01:11:35.749 --> 01:11:36.792
I don't want…

01:11:38.460 --> 01:11:39.795
I don't want it to be over.

01:11:41.463 --> 01:11:42.464
You're…

01:11:43.424 --> 01:11:45.009
You're my first love!

01:11:45.926 --> 01:11:47.052
I…

01:11:48.721 --> 01:11:50.681
I love you. You hear that?

01:11:51.849 --> 01:11:53.142
It's my first…
[sobs]

01:11:54.518 --> 01:11:57.479
I don't want to break up. Take me back.

01:12:00.024 --> 01:12:01.817
[dreamy music]

01:12:02.901 --> 01:12:04.278
[Yu-jin chuckles]

01:12:08.032 --> 01:12:09.199
Look at that.

01:12:11.618 --> 01:12:13.412
[chuckles]
There it is.

01:12:23.630 --> 01:12:25.007
[sighs]

01:12:29.762 --> 01:12:32.264
[Young-gil] It looks like we're getting
more snow than expected.

01:12:33.057 --> 01:12:35.184
We may need to run those numbers again.

01:12:35.267 --> 01:12:37.311
Should we get an update
on humidity report?

01:12:37.394 --> 01:12:39.063
Yeah, we should.

01:12:39.146 --> 01:12:41.398
Call Songwol-dong and ask
what's happening on their end.

01:12:41.482 --> 01:12:42.733
[employee 6] Okay.

01:12:52.868 --> 01:12:54.912
[dreamy music]

01:13:07.716 --> 01:13:10.636
Chan! Gyeol! Let's go.
We need to go to school.

01:13:10.719 --> 01:13:12.721
They're already on their way. Honey.

01:13:13.347 --> 01:13:15.474
Here. Drink this and get to work.

01:13:15.557 --> 01:13:17.017
- They're gone?
- Yeah.

01:13:17.518 --> 01:13:18.519
[chuckles]

01:13:22.481 --> 01:13:24.817
- Thanks, honey. See you soon.
- Mm-hm

01:13:26.985 --> 01:13:28.862
- Uh, honey?
- Huh?

01:13:29.988 --> 01:13:34.993
It's… You don't have to pass the exam,
so don't think we wouldn't be fine.

01:13:35.619 --> 01:13:36.912
What are you saying?

01:13:38.455 --> 01:13:42.209
If we had to go on like this,
I love you, so we'll be good.

01:13:44.294 --> 01:13:45.546
That's all.

01:13:45.629 --> 01:13:47.756
[bright music]

01:13:55.848 --> 01:13:58.642
- [Dong-han] Hey, can I help?
- Set the table.

01:13:58.725 --> 01:13:59.810
[Dong-han] Okay.

01:13:59.893 --> 01:14:02.646
[cutleries clinking]

01:14:08.944 --> 01:14:11.029
Bo-mi, breakfast is ready.

01:14:13.449 --> 01:14:15.951
I'm not hungry. I'm going to school.

01:14:17.911 --> 01:14:20.873
[door opens, closes]

01:14:20.956 --> 01:14:22.791
What's her deal? What did I do wrong?

01:14:23.709 --> 01:14:26.253
You're fine. She found out
her boy has a girlfriend.

01:14:26.336 --> 01:14:28.714
What boy? Who is he?

01:14:29.506 --> 01:14:32.092
Relax. It's a singer from a boy band.

01:14:32.176 --> 01:14:33.719
- You can sit.
- Okay.

01:14:34.887 --> 01:14:35.846
Singer?

01:14:40.100 --> 01:14:42.394
Well, this isn't so bad.

01:14:42.478 --> 01:14:43.604
[chuckles]

01:14:43.687 --> 01:14:45.772
[door lock chimes]

01:14:46.982 --> 01:14:48.066
[door closes]

01:14:55.699 --> 01:14:56.825
This is okay too, though.

01:14:56.909 --> 01:14:58.285
[chuckles]

01:14:58.368 --> 01:15:01.455
Dad, come on.
This isn't the time to laugh.

01:15:03.874 --> 01:15:04.875
Bo-mi.

01:15:05.751 --> 01:15:06.585
Are you good?

01:15:07.961 --> 01:15:10.506
[all chuckle]

01:15:10.589 --> 01:15:11.590
I'm good.

01:15:11.673 --> 01:15:14.301
If we expect precipitation,
we have to narrow down

01:15:14.384 --> 01:15:15.636
the type we'll see.

01:15:15.719 --> 01:15:17.221
[Soo-jin] If we expect snow or sleet,

01:15:17.304 --> 01:15:20.349
then we need to figure out when it'll
all start to stick to the ground.

01:15:20.974 --> 01:15:22.768
With snow, we'll also calculate

01:15:22.851 --> 01:15:25.103
the liquid water equivalent,
and expect a snowfall as well.

01:15:25.187 --> 01:15:28.649
You're expected to know all of this
if you work at the KMA.

01:15:28.732 --> 01:15:30.359
[trainees] Yes, ma'am.

01:15:30.442 --> 01:15:32.736
Who wrote the summer piece
that's on screen?

01:15:33.529 --> 01:15:34.905
"Seasonal Outlook"?

01:15:35.948 --> 01:15:36.782
I wrote it.

01:15:39.576 --> 01:15:43.664
I've told you before,
your title has to be sensational.

01:15:43.747 --> 01:15:46.124
Sensational things aren't good for kids.

01:15:47.793 --> 01:15:50.546
- You're taking your leave, right?
- Why wouldn't I? Of course, I will.

01:15:50.629 --> 01:15:52.005
When does that start?

01:15:52.089 --> 01:15:54.091
[sucks teeth]
I don't know.

01:15:54.174 --> 01:15:56.176
[clicks tongue]
The baby will let me know.

01:15:56.260 --> 01:15:58.053
- [chuckles]
- [scoffs]

01:15:58.136 --> 01:15:58.971
[Yu-jin grunts]

01:15:59.805 --> 01:16:03.517
I'll keep working until the day
this kid comes and I have to stop.

01:16:03.600 --> 01:16:05.519
You're really something.

01:16:05.602 --> 01:16:07.020
These days, I have to be.

01:16:07.688 --> 01:16:09.147
I'm a mom now.

01:16:10.941 --> 01:16:13.360
BACK IN MY DAY BY JIN TAE-KYUNG
SHIN SEOK-HO PUBLISHING COMPANY

01:16:15.404 --> 01:16:17.864
- What is that?
- [chuckles]

01:16:20.075 --> 01:16:23.245
Is it? It looks like my story.

01:16:24.621 --> 01:16:25.664
Uh…

01:16:25.747 --> 01:16:29.001
There's an option to self-publish, so…

01:16:30.085 --> 01:16:31.461
I published it.

01:16:33.463 --> 01:16:35.591
Yeah, maybe there's no conventional hook,

01:16:36.300 --> 01:16:38.802
but it has lots to offer in other ways.

01:16:40.429 --> 01:16:43.223
- Seok-ho.
- [chuckles]

01:16:46.018 --> 01:16:47.603
[Tae-kyung] Hang on. What's that?

01:16:48.937 --> 01:16:50.522
Oh, that? Uh…

01:16:51.148 --> 01:16:54.818
I'm going to publish
all your books from now on.

01:16:55.944 --> 01:16:58.572
- [giggling]
- Oh.

01:16:59.239 --> 01:17:01.867
How did I get a guy that's so awesome?

01:17:03.076 --> 01:17:05.662
So now I just have to…

01:17:06.622 --> 01:17:11.585
keep it up until your "guy"
turns into your "husband."

01:17:13.337 --> 01:17:15.631
- [giggles]
- Uh, Tae-kyung.

01:17:16.923 --> 01:17:19.092
[romantic music]

01:17:21.470 --> 01:17:22.929
Uh…

01:17:23.013 --> 01:17:26.391
Okay. See you later today.

01:17:26.975 --> 01:17:28.810
- See you tonight.
- Okay.

01:17:31.647 --> 01:17:32.939
[clanking]

01:17:39.571 --> 01:17:42.908
[Myung-han] Yeah. Hey, kid,
you're gonna be late?

01:17:43.492 --> 01:17:44.868
Uh, depends on the weather.

01:17:44.951 --> 01:17:47.996
Well, even if it's a nice day,
you shouldn't leave work early.

01:17:48.080 --> 01:17:49.289
You could stay out late.

01:17:50.165 --> 01:17:53.210
Uh, you could go on a date
with your Director Lady.

01:17:53.293 --> 01:17:54.169
Huh?

01:17:54.252 --> 01:17:56.421
[chuckles]
Don't forget your meds.

01:17:56.505 --> 01:17:59.466
And, hey, no more having all neighbors
over to play cards.

01:17:59.549 --> 01:18:01.051
Yeah, yeah, yeah. Go to work.

01:18:01.134 --> 01:18:02.719
And your chemo's in two days.

01:18:02.803 --> 01:18:06.264
I know when I have chemo.
Quit nagging. Come on.

01:18:06.348 --> 01:18:07.849
All right. See you later.

01:18:15.649 --> 01:18:16.775
[chuckles]

01:18:17.818 --> 01:18:19.695
Mm, if that's everyone, let's start.

01:18:21.321 --> 01:18:24.783
It is the 14th of March, 2023's
forecast meeting.

01:18:24.866 --> 01:18:26.284
Satellite Center, over to you.

01:18:26.368 --> 01:18:28.245
[employee 7]
Yes. This is Satellite Center.

01:18:28.328 --> 01:18:31.707
Currently, we're seeing yellow dust
in the West Sea… 

01:18:31.790 --> 01:18:38.797
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

01:18:46.471 --> 01:18:48.473
[light music]

01:19:04.948 --> 01:19:07.159
[inaudible dialogue]

01:19:26.178 --> 01:19:27.471
[Ha-kyung] I wonder

01:19:27.971 --> 01:19:32.017
if the answers in life
aren't a set constant from the start.

01:19:38.315 --> 01:19:42.819
They evolve over time and the choices
we make turn into the correct answers.

01:19:45.822 --> 01:19:50.952
So we shouldn't be afraid of making
a mistake or choosing the wrong thing.

01:19:55.415 --> 01:19:59.044
Because it still brings us closer
to the answer.

01:20:01.922 --> 01:20:04.674
I'll tell you tomorrow's forecast.

01:20:13.600 --> 01:20:14.643
Thank you.

01:20:18.897 --> 01:20:21.233
Uh, can you tell I'm nervous?

01:20:22.275 --> 01:20:24.236
Yes. It's obvious.

01:20:24.820 --> 01:20:25.946
What do I do?

01:20:26.029 --> 01:20:28.365
It's not too late.
We could abandon them and go back?

01:20:28.448 --> 01:20:31.409
No, we can't. I'm sure they've met by now.

01:20:31.493 --> 01:20:32.994
What do we do?

01:20:38.750 --> 01:20:40.544
- [exhales heavily]
- Oh, wait a sec.

01:20:43.547 --> 01:20:45.674
["Something Precious" by Rothy playing]

01:21:03.608 --> 01:21:04.818
What's this for?

01:21:06.027 --> 01:21:06.903
It's pretty.

01:21:07.988 --> 01:21:09.364
[chuckles]

01:21:10.574 --> 01:21:11.616
Let's go.

01:21:16.288 --> 01:21:18.540
Ah, it's nice to meet you.

01:21:19.124 --> 01:21:21.418
Director Jin Ha-kyung's
my youngest daughter,

01:21:21.501 --> 01:21:23.128
Bae Soo-ja. Pleasure.

01:21:23.211 --> 01:21:24.754
Uh, yes. How lovely to meet you.

01:21:25.547 --> 01:21:28.717
Of course, Lee Si-woo's my boy,
and I'm Lee Myung-han.

01:21:28.800 --> 01:21:30.051
[Myung-han chuckles]

01:21:30.594 --> 01:21:33.972
So, tell me,
has your chemotherapy gone well?

01:21:34.055 --> 01:21:35.724
Oh, yes, yes.

01:21:36.558 --> 01:21:40.520
We'll know it worked
if I stay healthy for the next few years.

01:21:40.604 --> 01:21:41.771
Ah.

01:21:41.855 --> 01:21:44.983
[Mrs. Bae] I can already tell,
he's a complete moron.

01:21:45.066 --> 01:21:48.653
[Myung-han] She's so cold she could
give a polar bear a freezer burn.

01:21:59.039 --> 01:22:01.541
Should we just go?

01:22:03.877 --> 01:22:04.753
Let's do it.

01:22:07.172 --> 01:22:09.299
[closing theme music]
